{
  "workers": [
    {
      "worker": 1,
      "brief": "You have rows 1‑20 of the ledger. Rows 1‑10 are the rate table (columns: row,rate_code,unit_rate). Rows 11‑20 are line items (columns: row,line_id,claim_id,qty,unit_rate,rate_code,paid). For each line item in your range, determine the applicable unit rate: use the line's unit_rate if it is non‑empty; otherwise look up the unit_rate for the given rate_code in the rate table (rows 1‑10). Compute amount_owed = qty × unit_rate. If paid < amount_owed, record this line as UNDERPAID and compute shortfall = amount_owed – paid (round to two decimals). Also record every claim_id you encounter. Output a JSON object with two arrays: \"underpaid\" (objects with row, line_id, claim_id, shortfall) and \"claims\" (list of claim_id strings you saw). Do not attempt to detect duplicates across workers; just list the claim_ids you have.",
